<title>USA: Sun Healthcare increases credit facility.</title>
<headline>Sun Healthcare increases credit facility.</headline>
<dateline>ALBUQUERQUE, N.M. 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sun Healthcare Group Inc said its board approved a $175 million increase in its bank credit facility, to $490 million from $315 million.</p>
<p>The long-term health-care company said it has borrowed $246 million of the $490 million now available.</p>
<p>The approval also includes an expansion of the lending group to 14 from nine firms, led by NationsBank of Texas N.A.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
